<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christian II, Count Palatine of Zweibrücken-Birkenfeld</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1637–1717</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christian II, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/count-palatine">Count Palatine</a> of Zweibrücken-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/birkenfeld">Birkenfeld</a>, ruled Birkenfeld, a minor branch of the Wittelsbach family, from 1654 until his death in 1717. Through his marriage to Catherine Agathe, heiress of the lords of Rappoltstein, he acquired the lordship of Rappoltstein (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lordship-of-rappoltstein">Ribeaupierre</a>) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> in 1673. His son Christian III later inherited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zweibrucken">Zweibrücken</a>, and the line moved there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christian-ii-count-palatine-of-zweibrucken-birkenfeld.jpg" alt="Christian II, Count Palatine of Zweibrücken-Birkenfeld" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Theodor Roos · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christian_II._(Pfalz-Zweibr%C3%BCcken-Birkenfeld).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
